dyadic block conclusion
  family maximum occurs at m=4: ratio=1371/4319 (0.317435), gap below 1/3=206/12957
  This is exactly the B30 new-speed maximum.

Interpretation
  The live post-gate constant is the 1/3 new-speed barrier.
  In B30 it is controlled by one dyadic block resonance:
    E'=(0,1,2,4,8,12,16,20), w=24, Delta^+/p1=1371/4319.
  Fold reciprocal mass helps locate the block but is not a monotone certificate:
    low-fold rows can still be moderately high, and high-fold rows can be harmless.
  The proof target should isolate dyadic block resonance first, then prove
  every other new-speed shell-full row has extra packet cancellation below 1/3.

